--- Part 7: candidate depth-interpolated spectrum vs shipped ---
The shipped spectrum has sigma_g > sigma_b at EVERY depth, so T is blue-leaning
everywhere (Part 1: g/b <= 0.96) and the cyan of the shallows can only come from a
warm bed. On a neutral bed the shallows read blue-teal (Part 4: hue 184.6).
Candidate: interpolate two ends by appearanceDepth, u = clamp((ad-1)/15, 0, 1);
  shallow end sigma_b > sigma_g  -> green survives -> cyan-green T;
  deep end    sigma_g >> sigma_b -> deep blue, wider gap than the shipped 0.04.

