Reading guide for the in-game pass:
  * the transmission's own hue is BLUE-leaning at every depth (g/b < 1) because
    green is absorbed faster than blue; that is the 2026-09-20 C1 re-ordering.
  * 'cyan' in the composed image therefore comes from the BED, not from the
    water: a warm sand bed multiplied by T keeps its green over blue and reads
    cyan; a neutral bed reads blue-teal at every depth (Part 4).
  * the deep end's blueness is set by the green-blue sigma gap: Astra BALANCED
    0.040/block vs Steadfast 0.125/block, i.e. 0.32x weaker (Part 2/5).
